The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
- `test_basic` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to crash with an IndexError when there was only one word

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split array.
